{"id":"CVE-2019-5737","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"nodejs","published":"2019-03-28T16:20:28.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T20:01:52.386Z","description":"In Node.js including 6.x before 6.17.0, 8.x before 8.15.1, 10.x before 10.15.2, and 11.x before 11.10.1, an attacker can cause a Denial of Service (DoS) by establishing an HTTP or HTTPS connection in keep-alive mode and by sending headers very slowly. This keeps the connection and associated resources alive for a long period of time. Potential attacks are mitigated by the use of a load balancer or other proxy layer. This vulnerability is an extension of CVE-2018-12121, addressed in November and impacts all active Node.js release lines including 6.x before 6.17.0, 8.x before 8.15.1, 10.x before 10.15.2, and 11.x before 11.10.1.","cwe":["CWE-400 CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption / Denial of Service"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Node.js","product":"Node.js","versions":["affected All versions prior to 6.17.0","affected All versions prior to 8.15.1","affected All versions prior to 10.15.2","affected All versions prior to 11.10.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/february-2019-security-releases/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-03/msg00041.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1076"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-04/msg00046.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1173"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-04/msg00059.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1211"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190502-0008/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:1821","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:1821"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202003-48","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202003-48"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-5739","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"nodejs","published":"2019-03-28T16:27:34.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T20:01:52.297Z","description":"Keep-alive HTTP and HTTPS connections can remain open and inactive for up to 2 minutes in Node.js 6.16.0 and earlier. Node.js 8.0.0 introduced a dedicated server.keepAliveTimeout which defaults to 5 seconds. The behavior in Node.js 6.16.0 and earlier is a potential Denial of Service (DoS) attack vector. Node.js 6.17.0 introduces server.keepAliveTimeout and the 5-second default.","cwe":["CWE-400 CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption / Denial of Service"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Node.js","product":"Node.js","versions":["affected All versions prior to 6.17.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/february-2019-security-releases/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-03/msg00041.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1076"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-04/msg00046.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1173"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190502-0008/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202003-48","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202003-48"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
