{"id":"CVE-2019-17625","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-10-16T11:07:36.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T01:47:13.423Z","description":"There is a stored XSS in Rambox 0.6.9 that can lead to code execution. The XSS is in the name field while adding/editing a service. The problem occurs due to incorrect sanitization of the name field when being processed and stored. This allows a user to craft a payload for Node.js and Electron, such as an exec of OS commands within the onerror attribute of an IMG element.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/ramboxapp/community-edition/issues/2418","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2019-19729","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-12-11T19:56:01.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T02:25:12.561Z","description":"An issue was discovered in the BSON ObjectID (aka bson-objectid) package 1.3.0 for Node.js. ObjectID() allows an attacker to generate a malformed objectid by inserting an additional property to the user-input, because bson-objectid will return early if it detects _bsontype==ObjectID in the user-input object. As a result, objects in arbitrary forms can bypass formatting if they have a valid bsontype.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/williamkapke/bson-objectid/issues/30","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/bson-objectid","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
